00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.940
So instead, we're
going to make a change

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.970
to make this more
politically correct.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:50.260
So I could do this
some from my machine.

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:53.236
I'm going to just
edit the file here.

00:06:53.236 --> 00:06:56.970
And Edit This File.

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.390
I'm going to make
a small change.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.760
Game 2.

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:04.970
And I'm going to say no lasers.

00:07:04.970 --> 00:07:09.572
And no, I want to
create a pull request.

00:07:09.572 --> 00:07:14.730
And this would to go through my
typical process of code review

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.460
that we're going to skip
today, because I know

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:19.440
this is going to work for sure.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.760
[LAUGHTER]

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:26.340
So what's going to happen
is, as you see here,

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.190
I have a bot that has
commented in my pull request.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.660
It is basically telling me this
pull request is not approved.

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:37.610
This is a bot that is
included in Jenkins X.

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:40.070
And I can talk to this bot.

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:44.810
And I can say things, very
important things, like meow.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:53.270
And my bot is going
to answer back to me.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:54.200
So I can do--

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.295
I can talk to this bot.

00:07:55.295 --> 00:07:56.420
There are several commands.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:57.830
This is using Prow.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.990
This is a project
from Kubernetes itself

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:03.170
that they use for
CI/CD of Kubernetes.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:05.965
So this is basically
listening to web hook events

00:08:05.965 --> 00:08:07.700
and doing things.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.740
You can write your own plugins.

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:13.880
And you can see here, there
is a serverless Jenkins--

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:17.470
and I'm going to talk a
little bit about that soon--

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:20.520
and type checks that
are still running.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:27.240
So if I go to my Command
Line and I think this is--

00:08:29.890 --> 00:08:32.720
I want to check the logs.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:33.510
