00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:35.413
No.

00:08:35.413 --> 00:08:38.169
OK.

00:08:38.169 --> 00:08:42.640
So I can see the logs of the
build of this pull request

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:45.680
happening in Kubernetes.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:48.490
So this is used in
serverless Jenkins, which

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:53.410
is a project that we
created that allows you

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:57.580
to have several lists built.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:03.040
So every time there's a web hook
event coming into Jenkins X,

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.410
it will create a new
path for Jenkins.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:10.660
So it's a small Jenkins server
running that it doesn't--

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:12.473
it only takes a few
seconds to start.

00:09:12.473 --> 00:09:13.640
So it's not the whole thing.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:14.557
You don't need the UI.

00:09:14.557 --> 00:09:17.970
You don't need all
the extra things.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:21.150
And what is going to happen,
it's going to create the path,

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:26.300
run that, and at the end of the
build it's going to disappear.

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:29.560
So you have two options on
Jenkins X. You have the option

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:33.100
to have a static master like the
typical Jenkins that you know.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.780
And you have the
serverless option.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.790
And this is going to be using--

00:09:36.790 --> 00:09:39.760
pretty soon we're
integrating Tekton.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.820
If you heard about
Tekton the project,

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:46.090
it was talked about
in other sessions.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.520
It's coming from Knative build.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:52.750
And it's basically allowing
you to use containers in your

00:09:52.750 --> 00:09:55.130
build pipeline.

