00:24:05.740 --> 00:24:07.740
One thing I've
been working on is

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:11.690
to do a progressive delivery,
kind of redeployment.

00:24:11.690 --> 00:24:14.730
So progressive delivery
encompasses canary deployments,

00:24:14.730 --> 00:24:17.400
blue-green deployments,
things like that.

00:24:17.400 --> 00:24:21.150
So basically you don't
want to deploy new versions

00:24:21.150 --> 00:24:23.280
to all your users.

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:25.950
Because you don't know if
it's going to break something.

00:24:25.950 --> 00:24:28.150
You want to deploy it
to a subset of users.

00:24:28.150 --> 00:24:32.010
So this is the typical stuff
that Netflix, Facebook, Google

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:34.240
does.

00:24:34.240 --> 00:24:39.810
So what we're doing, and what
I have enabled in this project,

00:24:39.810 --> 00:24:43.210
is exactly that kind
of redeployment.

00:24:43.210 --> 00:24:47.350
So I have-- basically,
Jenkins X has

00:24:47.350 --> 00:24:51.430
the concept of applications,
Jenkins X applications

00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:53.230
or extension points.

00:24:53.230 --> 00:24:56.290
And one of them is Flagger.

00:24:56.290 --> 00:24:58.750
So Flagger is a
project that will

00:24:58.750 --> 00:25:02.270
do this kind of
redeployments for you.

00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:06.620
And this is using Istio
and Prometheus metrics.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:09.460
So what we're going
to see here is

00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:12.310
that Flagger detects there's
a new change, a change

00:25:12.310 --> 00:25:15.310
to my deployment in Kubernetes.

00:25:15.310 --> 00:25:22.940
And instead of switching
the whole traffic to it,

00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:26.270
it's going to create
the Istio deployment

00:25:26.270 --> 00:25:32.860
configuration necessary to shift
traffic a little at a time.

00:25:32.860 --> 00:25:34.260
So what we're going to do--

00:25:34.260 --> 00:25:35.550
I have it configured.

00:25:35.550 --> 00:25:37.000
It's going to do--
every minute is

00:25:37.000 --> 00:25:38.880
going to shift 10%
of the traffic, so

00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:41.700
10%, 20%, 30%, 40%, and 50%.

00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:45.580
And then at 50 it's going
to deploy to everybody else.

00:25:45.580 --> 00:25:49.030
So we're going to see that
in the logs in a second.

00:25:49.030 --> 00:25:55.010
